 "background": [
  {
   "text": "Three levels of reconfiguration: alternate law (with or without reduced protections), direct law, mechanical. The ECAM and PFD indicate any control law degradation.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-27-20-20",
     "page": "P 1/20",
     "pdf": 1612
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "In flight, pitch alternate law is based on load factor demand; the basic high speed protection, pitch attitude protection and angle-of-attack protection are not available.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-27-20-20",
     "page": "P 11/20",
     "pdf": 1622
    },
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-27-20-20",
     "page": "P 14/20",
     "pdf": 1625
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Alternate law without reduced protection: identical to alternate law but without the low-speed or high-speed stability — only the load factor limitation remains.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-27-20-20",
     "page": "P 17/20",
     "pdf": 1628
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Low energy aural alert is lost in alternate law.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "PDP",
     "code": "Reconfiguration laws",
     "page": "EFTDN1RCFGLAW01",
     "pdf": 514
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The AP disconnects if the speed exceeds VMO/MMO or the bank angle exceeds 45°.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-27-20-20",
     "page": "P 13/20",
     "pdf": 1624
    },
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-27-20-20",
     "page": "P 16/20",
     "pdf": 1627
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "If the aircraft goes far outside the normal envelope, the abnormal attitude law engages (F/CTL DIRECT LAW on ECAM); after recovery, alternate law without reduced protection remains for the rest of the flight (F/CTL ALTN LAW on ECAM).",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-27-20-20",
     "page": "P 18/20",
     "pdf": 1629
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "technique": [
  {
   "text": "Within the normal flight envelope, alternate-law handling in pitch is identical to normal law. Outside it, the PF must take appropriate preventive actions to avoid losing control or high speed excursions.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "AOP-10-30-20",
     "page": "P 1/2",
     "pdf": 62
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "At high altitude, descend about 4 000 ft below REC MAX ALT to reduce stall warnings in turbulence. At high speed, maneuver with care using small inputs.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "AOP-10-30-20",
     "page": "P 1/2",
     "pdf": 62
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Protections are not structural limits; the PF must not deliberately exceed the normal flight envelope.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "AOP-10-30-10",
     "page": "P 1/2",
     "pdf": 60
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Direct law: be careful with large thrust changes or sudden speedbrake movements, particularly with an aft CG. Retract speedbrakes gently to give time to re-trim. At go-around, TOGA thrust gives a large pitch-up moment — apply nose-down trim to avoid excessive pitch-up or a transient stall warning.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "AOP-10-30-20",
     "page": "P 1/2",
     "pdf": 62
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
